From 884b2bb6dea723a5c87619ee340f2c77f7b2bb2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:28:21 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 02/23] CUDA keyed graph cache and device arena, both off until
 a family installs them.

graph_cache.Cache captures one executable graph per caller-named key and replays it when the key comes back; ranks agree on every capture, eviction and fallback through an Agree hook, and a memory floor turns misses eager.
arena.Arena sub-allocates DeviceBuffer.alloc from a few large chunks (VMM or plain cuMemAlloc) through memory.setHook; borrowed spans and pointers it does not own are freed as before.

(cherry picked from commit 986c996041e25e8b4a0341a8b54524a9d2248c12)
